e will teach the same thing but you will feel a little different. Okay. So now that we understand why LLM evaluations are important. And how LLM evaluations are different from software testing. Now let's move on to the main topic of the day. What are LLM evals? We have not discussed this yet. I mean we have done it from the top but let's read it in detail. Okay. So here I have written a definition. I will first read the definition and then we will discuss the point. So we can define LLM evals as. That LLM evals are systematic repeatable tests. Used to judge an LLM or LLM powered system against a clear criteria. Okay. Basically LLM evaluations are tests. Which we apply on LLM or LLM based applications\"]}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Contextual Recall", "threshold": 0.7, "success": false, "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile", "evaluationCost": 0}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": false}}, {"metric_data": {"name": "Contextual Precision", "threshold": 0.7, "success": false, "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile", "evaluationCost": 0}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": false}}]}, "{\"actual_output\": \"(generator not evaluated in this run)\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": \"No\\u2014you generally don't select a single model directly from a leaderboard. Leaderboards are best used as a filtering tool: when you don't have the resources to run evals on hundreds of models yourself, you go to the relevant leaderboard (say the maths leaderboard if your app is in the maths domain), pick your top candidates, and shortlist from the hundred down to about five. Then you run your own evals on those shortlisted candidates and select the best one for your application from the