ent eval methods through which we perform evaluations. We discussed three things in this video. Programmatic methods, LLMEvalse-based as a judge, and how to perform eval with humans. In nutshell, this is the summary of whatever we have covered in this course till now. In today's video, we are going to discuss a very important topic. The topic is Offline Eval vs Online Eval. First, I will tell you what is offline eval, then I will tell you what is online eval, and then what are the differences between them. We will see that and you will learn a lot in this process. This is our agenda for today. This is the topic that we are going to cover today\", \". I will give you an example of this, I will give you an example of this, The statement I said, Offline eval tells correctness, Online eval tells normalcy, I will give you an example of this, Remember our UPSC grader, Who checks the paper, Remember our UPSC grader, Can you tell me, When we were discussing in the last class, Offline evaluation of this system, When we were discussing in the last class, So what were we doing exactly? So what were we doing exactly? What were we trying to do? When we were applying offline eval, What were we trying to do? What were we trying to do? We discussed in great detail that What are the purposes we were trying to solve? Do you remember In the last session, We discussed UPSC grader, We discussed in great detail there that Our grader, Now this grader that\", \". The simplest definition of online eval is, That it is a different type of evaluation, Which we run on production, After our software is deployed. And the biggest characteristic of it is, That it works without an answer. It works without a golden data set. This is the biggest feature of online eval. And that is why it is super critical, Because it helps us, That our software, which is deployed, Keeps running properly. It tells us that, There is no problem with online. In that sense, online evals are super important. So, on the basi